{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792800304,"nonce":"qhk0nnXhxXcDEqr2W85PFYoIFAw=","message":"Implemented the local recovery slice. Each workspace document gets a locked recovery folder, a checksummed full Yrs update-v1 snapshot, and a checksummed update journal. Updates are flushed on the native worker before local-save markers and before host acknowledgement/broadcast. Logs compact after 128 records or 512 KiB, have a 4 MiB ceiling, and retain CRDT identity/clocks, deletion sets and pending out-of-order updates. Snapshot publication is atomic; sequence numbers handle a crash before journal truncation. Partial final frames are discarded; complete corruption and oversize logs fail without silent replacement. Storage errors stop acknowledgement and poison the store against subsequent writes.\n\nProtocol v2 advertises stable document identity and host durability, rejects mismatched rooms before merging, and explicitly rejects protocol v1. Recovery files contain source state but no invitation secret or display name. Resuming rotates the invitation. Resume Saved Document and Rejoin Saved Document require explicit action and a clean buffer; fresh start/join prompts explain replacing the previous checkpoint. No automatic connection or source-file writes. Per-author undo starts fresh after process restart. Jam status exposes local-save progress; its menu offers an explicit checkpoint. Accepted queued local writes drain on the worker when leaving.\n\nValidation: 14 native tests on macOS ARM64 and Linux x86_64 NUC; clippy all-targets with warnings denied; local and macOS/NUC peer checks; actual host/guest process exits followed by durable offline merge, secret rotation, stable identity and unrelated-room rejection. The NUC was checked idle before two low-priority build jobs. Editor integration passed in both themes under hybrid and AOT, including dirty-buffer guard, explicit resume/rejoin, source-file preservation, Unicode ranges, per-author undo/redo, IME deferral, caret stability, inactive view release and cleanup. Snapshot reviewed. Complete scripts/check-jam.sh --ssh nuc --remote-binary /tmp/rayde-jam-20261024/target/debug/rayde-jam passed; logs in bin/jam-final-check.log and bin/jam-recovery-aot-check.log. RayDE bytecode/AOT executable rebuilt; existing AOT app updated with the rebuilt executable and native library, re-signed and verified with codesign --deep --strict.\n\nThis does not close the wider recovery roadmap: hosted durability, account identity, room discovery, epoch reset/compaction, durable collaborative undo across restarts, asset/filesystem replication, and Cloudflare/media integration remain open. Backup/restore is available by copying the whole recovery folder while the Jam is stopped. Edits still marked saving when a process dies are not guaranteed durable. This change was not pushed.","files":null}]}